# Phase J (spec §37, §21; ADR-0050): the remote-link overview is `get link | view table` — not a
# command of its own. Both halves were proven separately (`049-remote-link` for the link table,
# `075-adapters-interactive-table` for the renderer) and the composition by nothing, which is
# the one thing a user actually types. The link is made against this very binary over a pipe
# pair, so the case needs no network — the suite runs with networking disabled.
case: the link overview is a table of links, browsed in the view
pty: true
columns: 100
lines: 30
timeout: 90
env: NO_COLOR=1
stdin: |
  link host testbox --transport local
  link host otherbox --transport local
  get link | view table
  q
  get link | count
  exit
run: |
  ono
exit: 0
stdout-contains: linked testbox (local)
stdout-contains: [up/down] move
stdout-matches: testbox +testbox +local
stdout-matches: otherbox +otherbox +local
stdout-not-contains: panicked
stdout-not-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0101
